    </categories>
    <contentRows>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "dd183f78-7d69-4eda-9b4c-a25970583a28",
      "key": "9b9ff1e9-3f40-4692-8a99-b9a35296299e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003E\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;The ProWorks team is excited to announce the release of TinyMCE.Umbraco v17, our latest update to the \u0026lt;a rel=\u0026quot;noopener\u0026quot; href=\u0026quot;https://github.com/ProWorksCorporation/TinyMCE-Umbraco\u0026quot; target=\u0026quot;_blank\u0026quot;\u0026gt;TinyMCE.Umbraco package\u0026lt;/a\u0026gt; for Umbraco CMS. If you\u0026#39;re using or upgrading to Umbraco 17 and want to continue using TinyMCE, this update ensures full compatibility with the new Web Components-based back-office and adds in some other great features as well:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Additional features include:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Streamlined configuration for RTE Data Types in Umbraco\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Enhanced settings that support direct JSON-based configuration via .NET (\u0026lt;code\u0026gt;appsettings.json\u0026lt;/code\u0026gt;)\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Support for updating TinyMCE to versions 7 or 8\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Simple configuration-based TinyMCE Premium setup\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;OpenAI and ChatGPT integrations out-of-the-box\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Migrations from v15 that keep TinyMCE in Umbraco as an RTE option by default\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;More information and documentation about TinyMCE.Umbraco here: \u0026lt;a rel=\u0026quot;noopener\u0026quot; href=\u0026quot;https://github.com/ProWorksCorporation/TinyMCE-Umbraco\u0026quot; target=\u0026quot;_blank\u0026quot;\u0026gt;https://github.com/ProWorksCorporation/TinyMCE-Umbraco\u0026lt;/a\u0026gt;\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;h2\u0026gt;Highlights from the Umbraco 17 Release\u0026lt;/h2\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Umbraco version 17 includes several major improvements that make it a compelling upgrade for most teams:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;h3\u0026gt;Umbraco MCP Server\u0026lt;/h3\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;A new integration layer to enable content editors to report on, manage, create, and update content and media through AI chat interfaces like ChatGPT and Claude. This allows for bulk operations and reporting where AI can reason and help editors understand their content at a new level.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;h3\u0026gt;Enhanced caching configuration\u0026lt;/h3\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;The new caching layer allows for more fine-grained configuration. Instead of simply caching all the content, now it can cache only the most used content for faster startup times and better performance for sites with lots of content.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;h3\u0026gt;A fully rebuilt back-office\u0026lt;/h3\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;The new back-office UI is powered by standard JavaScript Web Components, delivering better performance, faster load times, and a more modern foundation for custom extensions.\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Read the official announcement from Umbraco here: \u0026lt;a rel=\u0026quot;noopener\u0026quot; href=\u0026quot;https://umbraco.com/blog/umbraco-17-lts-release/\u0026quot; target=\u0026quot;_blank\u0026quot;\u0026gt;https://umbraco.com/blog/umbraco-17-lts-release/\u0026lt;/a\u0026gt;\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;h2\u0026gt;Thinking about upgrading?\u0026lt;/h2\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;We\u2019d be happy to help with:\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Upgrading from Umbraco versions 8 - 16 to the latest LTS\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Back-office extension development\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Custom TinyMCE plugins or editor integrations\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;Modernizing workflows using MCP Server and AI-enabled tooling\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;li\u0026gt;Custom MCP implementations for Umbraco websites\u0026lt;/li\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/ul\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;p\u0026gt;If you\u2019d like to discuss your upgrade strategy or schedule a brief consultation, \u0026lt;a href=\u0026quot;#section-footer\u0026quot; data-anchor=\u0026quot;#section-footer\u0026quot;\u0026gt;contact us below\u0026lt;/a\u0026gt; and we would be happy to help!\u0026lt;/p\u0026gt;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://www.proworks.com/blog/archive/tinymceumbraco-v17-released-and-ready-for-umbraco-17/\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
